{
  "core_question": "How to design a defensible first version of an AI sepsis risk score clinical decision support tool for a 12-hospital system, covering clinical safety, legal/regulatory exposure, and financial structure.",
  "rationale": "The project requires expertise in clinical validation and workflow integration (healthcare), regulatory classification, liability, and data governance (legal), and pricing strategy, cost modeling, and reimbursement considerations (finance).",
  "routes": ["healthcare", "legal", "finance"],
  "sub_questions": {
    "healthcare": "For a 12-hospital health system deploying an AI sepsis risk score CDS tool via per-seat annual subscription, what are the key clinical safety requirements—including data quality controls, model validation protocols, real‑time monitoring, and clinician workflow integration—to ensure patient safety and maintain regulatory compliance in the first version?",
    "legal": "Given a 12-hospital health system using an AI sepsis risk score CDS tool on a per-seat subscription basis, what legal and regulatory steps must be taken to classify the product under FDA guidance, address HIPAA data privacy, manage liability for clinical decisions, and structure contracts with providers to mitigate exposure?",
    "finance": "For a 12-hospital health system rolling out an AI sepsis risk score CDS tool via per-seat annual subscription, what financial model should be used to price the service, allocate costs between capital and operating expenses, estimate ROI, and account for potential reimbursement or cost‑savings benefits?"
  },
  "requires_recency_disclosure": true,
  "recency_notes": "Recent FDA guidance on AI/ML medical devices, evolving CMS reimbursement policies for CDS tools, and updated HIPAA privacy rule interpretations may affect the answers."
}
